            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, the case presents two disparate views of what kind of loss is necessary to sustain a claim for securities fraud under the Reform Act's loss\u2011causation requirement."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7beac3d65f5593c896838e8eb0985d6c2e798675ecd54e1d080318e0aeb33143",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7beac3d65f55-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked whether, had certiorari not been granted, the Ninth Circuit\u2019s opinion would have become final and what would have happened on remand and in the trial court."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7beac3d65f5593c896838e8eb0985d6c2e798675ecd54e1d080318e0aeb33143",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7beac3d65f55-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice O'Connor, justice O'Connor questioned whether the general pleading rule governing complaints was adequate for securities\u2011fraud cases."
      }
    ],
